Title: Sleep and the simulation clock of /Verse.org/Simulation work in verse.exe

verse.exe has no UWorld, so it has no Sleep, and GetSecondsSinceEpoch returns the start time for the whole run,
because the engine updates it at the start of each frame and verse.exe never starts one. This patch links Epic's
VerseSimulation module, which declares Sleep and GetSimulationElapsedTime, and replaces their UWorld-based bodies
through the hooks that VerseSimulation provides for programs without a world. A frame is one job of the event loop,
and when the loop has no job left it waits for the task in Sleep that is due first. The simulation clock advances
by that wait and by at most 0.25 seconds for each job, so time spent stopped at a breakpoint barely counts.

